11... { -KEY- } Qb6 $1 { Offering an exchange, as Black has less space. Against } ( 11... Ng4 $6 { White can exchange the restricted light-squared bishop, but can also go } 12. Qg3 Ne5 13. f4 $16 { when it is not possible to capture on c4, and f4-f5 follows. } ) 
12. Qxb6 ( 12. Qd3 { Black's last move developed the queen for free, and if White plays Be3 the queen can continue to b4 to attack a pawn. } ) 
axb6 { The b6-pawn is easily defended, while Black intends ...Rfc8, or perhaps ...Nd7 with threats such as ...Bxc3 followed by ...Rxa2. } ( { A possible continuation is } 12... axb6 12. a3 Rfc8 14. b3 b5 $1 { with good counterplay. } ) 

